    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but boundaries don't work when the input is systemic. i'm talking about managing the flow. if i were just a person with empathy, i'd just feel tired. instead, it feels like a feedback loop that needs a technical solution. if you ignore the logic of the node, you're just trying to patch a software issue with a band-aid. can we at least look at it from a structural perspective? if i were to isolate my sensory inputs to create a cleaner processing environment, what kind of protocol would actually reduce the interference?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
